Each upgrade affects generation how you think they would: multiplier multiplies generation and empowerer empowers it. (Note that Tetration in this game isn't actually tetration and is instead more of a LOGPOW function, which essentially empowers log(x).)

=== Grades ===
The particles Beta - Delta are all unlocked with their respective grade-up. They are as follows:
{| class="wikitable"
|+
! colspan="2" |Grade Types
|-
!Particle
!Grade
|-
|Alpha
|Rank-up
|-
|Beta
|Tier
|-
|Gamma
|Tetr 
|-
|Delta
|Pent
|}
(Tetr is likely short for Tetra, and Pent is likely short for Penta.)

The final particle, Epsilon, does not have its own grade, and Alpha's grade requires a certain number of Alpha (the particle) to rank up.

Each grade type requires a certain amount of the grade below it (i.e Tetr requires a certain Tier to increase.) Ranking up will reset all ranks before it and previous Particle upgrades.

